\section{Flags}{

\code{flag} takes one of four fixed strings, assigned in this precedence order
so a cell that qualifies for more than one gets the most serious:
\enumerate{
\item \code{"Dead (>95\% zero)"} — \code{pct_zero_mean > dead_pct_zero}. A cell that is
unloaded in almost every frame of every recording is not measuring
zero pressure, it is not measuring. Dead cells depress the whole-grid
mean (\code{\link[=pr_calc_mean_pressure_grid]{pr_calc_mean_pressure_grid()}}) and are invisible to the
loaded-cells-only \code{\link[=pr_calc_mean_pressure]{pr_calc_mean_pressure()}}.
\item \code{"Saturated (>60 kPa)"} — \code{max_across_files >= saturation_kpa}. The
cell reached the hardware ceiling, so its true peak is unknown and
censored from above. Any peak-derived cohort number
(\code{\link[=pr_calc_pci]{pr_calc_pci()}}, \code{peak_kPa_max}) is a lower bound wherever these
cells carry the hotspot.
\item \code{"Low variance"} — \code{sd_across_files < low_var_sd}. The cell responds,
but barely: a plausible stuck or half-detached cell that is not zero
often enough to read as dead.
\item \code{"OK"} — none of the above.
